PTPA
XScreenSaver doesn't play nicely with Wayland. This setup works around that with four small scripts and swayidle.

What they do:
--------------
1. Watch how long you've been idle
2. Pick a random screensaver from your list
3. Force it fullscreen through a KDE window rule
4. When you come back: restore brightness and lock the session

What you can tweak:
--------------------
1. Idle timeout — change IDLE_TIMEOUT in run-screensaver.sh (minutes, default 1)
2. Resume behavior — remove the loginctl lock-session line from resume-handler.sh if you don't want it to lock

Dependencies:
--------------
Install the following
1. xscreensaver
2. swayidle
3. pactl
4. brightnessctl

Setup to run screensavers in full screen in KDE 6.3:
-----------------------------------------------------
1. Run one screensaver application in your screensavers folder then
right click on the title bar then click configure special application settings
in More Actions with the following settings:
2. Window class (application) field = substring match for "screensaver-"
3. Match whole window class field = Yes
4. Window type field = All selected
5. Fullscreen Size & Position property = Force; Yes

Final steps
------------
1. Save the four scripts in ~/Documents/bin:
   a. build-screensaver-symlinks.sh
   b. run-screensaver.sh
   c. random-screensaver.sh
   d. resume-handler.sh

   Then make them executable:
   chmod +x ~/Documents/bin/*.sh
2. Run the build-screensaver-symlinks.sh script to create the symlinks in ~/Documents/screensaver/ that point to the real binaries in /usr/libexec/xscreensaver/
3. Add the run-screensaver.sh script as a login script in Autostart KDE Settings


